            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="0354" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1431/76: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-29T12:00:00-06:00">September 29,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. Department’s telegram No. 58, September 28, 6 p.m.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d298-f1"/> The Minister for Foreign Affair’s has just told me that
                    the agreement will go into effect immediately on signature by President Ubico
                    acting under his extraordinary powers but must be submitted to the Legislative
                    Assembly for ratification when it convenes next March.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
